<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ayurbarwada Buyantu Khan</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1285">1285</a>–<a href="/years/1320">1320</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> · Also known as Emperor Renzong of Yuan</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ayurbarwada Buyantu Khan, known by the temple name Renzong, was emperor of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yuan-dynasty">Yuan dynasty</a> from 1311 to 1320. Educated in Confucian learning, he favoured Chinese-style government, curbed some abuses of his predecessor's reign and in 1315 restored the civil service examinations, although with quotas that favoured <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongols">Mongols</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/semu">Semu</a>. He was succeeded by his son Shidebala.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ayurbarwada-buyantu-khan.jpg" alt="Ayurbarwada Buyantu Khan" width="320" height="404" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: AnonymousUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:YuanEmperorAlbumAyurbarvadaBuyantuPortrait.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
